@startuml UC-72 Hide Comment on Own Content - Sequence Diagram (icon)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title 2.10.2.10 UC-72 Hide Comment on Own Content — Sequence Diagram

actor Teacher
boundary ":CommunityHubDetailPage" as UI
control ":HubContentController" as CTL
control ":HubCommentService" as SVC
boundary ":HubCommentRepository" as COMMENTS
boundary ":LibraryContentRepository" as CONTENTS
database DB

autonumber
Teacher ->> UI : Click "Hide" on another teacher's comment on their own Hub content
activate UI
UI -->> Teacher : Show the hide confirmation dialog (MSG44)
Teacher ->> UI : Click "Hide comment" to confirm
UI ->> UI : confirmDeleteComment()
UI ->> CTL : POST /api/hub/comments/{commentId}/hide
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : hideByContentOwner(commentId)
activate SVC

SVC ->> COMMENTS : findById(commentId)
activate COMMENTS
COMMENTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM hub_content_comments WHERE id = ?
activate DB
DB -->> COMMENTS : row / none
deactivate DB
COMMENTS -->> SVC : HubComment
deactivate COMMENTS

SVC ->> CONTENTS : findApprovedForHubById(libraryContentId)
activate CONTENTS
CONTENTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM library_contents WHERE id = ? AND status = 'APPROVED' AND deleted_at IS NULL
activate DB
DB -->> CONTENTS : row / none
deactivate DB
CONTENTS -->> SVC : LibraryContent
deactivate CONTENTS

alt the content or comment is unavailable, the comment is the requester's own, or the requester does not own the content
  SVC -->> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException / IllegalArgumentException / ForbiddenOperationException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 404 / 400 / 403
  UI -->> Teacher : Show that hiding is not permitted and leave the comment visible

else the requester owns the content and the comment belongs to another teacher
  SVC ->> COMMENTS : save(comment)
  activate COMMENTS
  COMMENTS ->> DB : UPDATE hub_content_comments SET hidden_at = ?, hidden_by = ? WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB -->> COMMENTS : Saved
  deactivate DB
  COMMENTS -->> SVC : HubComment
  deactivate COMMENTS
  SVC ->> SVC : load the visible comments of that content and soft-hide every direct reply of the root comment the same way
  SVC -->> CTL : void
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 204 No Content
  UI -->> Teacher : Show MSG45 and the discussion without the hidden comment and its replies
end

deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
